{
  "case_id": "2001-00-568",
  "document_hash": "d335501401b3d8804c6a1f43bb23e49f997234e7915398e825ed1088184a0038",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2001-00-568",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d335501401b3d8804c6a1f43bb23e49f997234e7915398e825ed1088184a0038",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d335501401b3-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:02 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-00-568",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d335501401b3d8804c6a1f43bb23e49f997234e7915398e825ed1088184a0038",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d335501401b3-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: What if there -- what if there were no statute at all? Do you think that under the Commerce Clause, with today's multi-state grids for transmission of power, that the States could have directly regulated energy transmission as a separate service?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-00-568",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d335501401b3d8804c6a1f43bb23e49f997234e7915398e825ed1088184a0038",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d335501401b3-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Did it say it had no jurisdiction or just chose, in its discretion, not to regulate them?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice (unspecified)",
      "case_id": "2001-00-568",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d335501401b3d8804c6a1f43bb23e49f997234e7915398e825ed1088184a0038",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d335501401b3-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: And you agree with that? You agree it was a policy choice and not a jurisdiction --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent (Mr. Cohen)",
      "case_id": "2001-00-568",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d335501401b3d8804c6a1f43bb23e49f997234e7915398e825ed1088184a0038",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d335501401b3-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We think that the States have plenary power to regulate who may serve their retail customers and at what rates and at what -- and on what other terms and conditions. But they must take into account FERC's -- and properly respect FERC's regulation of the -- the item that is within FERC's jurisdiction, namely transmission."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent (Mr. Kneedler)",
      "case_id": "2001-00-568",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d335501401b3d8804c6a1f43bb23e49f997234e7915398e825ed1088184a0038",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d335501401b3-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Order 888 fully respects and, indeed, complements State regulatory jurisdiction over the transmission -- excuse me -- over the sale of electric energy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-00-568",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d335501401b3d8804c6a1f43bb23e49f997234e7915398e825ed1088184a0038",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d335501401b3-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Where are you reading from?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State",
      "case_id": "2001-00-568",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d335501401b3d8804c6a1f43bb23e49f997234e7915398e825ed1088184a0038",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d335501401b3-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the State, in setting a retail rate -- as Mr. Cohen explained,\nthe State in setting a retail rate, would have to take\ninto account all of the costs that are components of that\nretail rate. That could be the cost of the electric\nenergy, the commodity, and it would also include,\nimportantly, the cost of the transmission service."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "FERC",
      "case_id": "2001-00-568",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d335501401b3d8804c6a1f43bb23e49f997234e7915398e825ed1088184a0038",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d335501401b3-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "FERC would have the power under the wholesale sales clause, it would unquestionably, we think, have the power under the transmission clause, which I said is a -- is a --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Enron",
      "case_id": "2001-00-568",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d335501401b3d8804c6a1f43bb23e49f997234e7915398e825ed1088184a0038",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d335501401b3-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What Enron is seeking here is to have an existing regulation on open access, all comers, anytime, anywhere to -- for retail -- excuse me -- to have a -- a pricing provision under an open access regime applied to the -- the transmission component even in the monopoly State."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "FERC",
      "case_id": "2001-00-568",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d335501401b3d8804c6a1f43bb23e49f997234e7915398e825ed1088184a0038",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d335501401b3-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "FERC does have jurisdiction, but FERC, in exercising that jurisdiction, could say, we do not wish to exercise it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-00-568",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d335501401b3d8804c6a1f43bb23e49f997234e7915398e825ed1088184a0038",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d335501401b3-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "One is a question of power. Does FERC have the power to do it? One is a question of should it exercise that power, the policy question. Which is no power and which is a matter of policy?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-00-568",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d335501401b3d8804c6a1f43bb23e49f997234e7915398e825ed1088184a0038",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d335501401b3-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: If you have the power to characterize it one way or the other, it seems to me you have the power to assert jurisdiction. So, you're saying FERC has the power to assert jurisdiction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "FERC",
      "case_id": "2001-00-568",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d335501401b3d8804c6a1f43bb23e49f997234e7915398e825ed1088184a0038",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d335501401b3-0003-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KNEEDLER: As a Chevron matter, FERC has -- has concluded -- has construed the statute not to authorize it to -- under Chevron, the -- the agency could go either way."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-00-568",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d335501401b3d8804c6a1f43bb23e49f997234e7915398e825ed1088184a0038",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d335501401b3-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Mr. Kneedler, may I ask you this question? If we assume -- we assume the commission has said that they do not have jurisdiction when the transaction remains bundled, because it wasn't voluntarily unbundled or compelled to be unbundled by State or Federal authority. If we disagreed with that and said, no, you do have jurisdiction there, is there anything in the statute that would compel them to exercise the jurisdiction?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-00-568",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d335501401b3d8804c6a1f43bb23e49f997234e7915398e825ed1088184a0038",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d335501401b3-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: It's all at the sufferance of FERC, however. I mean, in FERC's graciousness, it -- it allows the -- the State of New York to decide who should be served first, and if FERC wanted to change that and say, we say these should be your priority -- right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "FERC",
      "case_id": "2001-00-568",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d335501401b3d8804c6a1f43bb23e49f997234e7915398e825ed1088184a0038",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d335501401b3-0003-0007",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I'm informed by FERC that there are virtually none anymore, and that -- that while the act does preserve intrastate transmission to the -- to the States, there's virtually none that isn't connected to the grid."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-00-568",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d335501401b3d8804c6a1f43bb23e49f997234e7915398e825ed1088184a0038",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d335501401b3-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Would you say that if a State regulates a bundled retail sale, it is, for all practical purposes, in part regulating transmission?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2001-00-568",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d335501401b3d8804c6a1f43bb23e49f997234e7915398e825ed1088184a0038",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d335501401b3-0003-0008",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
